/* Strategic command: fly the route that is already set.
 *
 * Succeeds when no route remains and, for a leg that ordered a dock, the
 * ship is actually docked — that is what "the route has been flown" looks
 * like from the outside, and a route to a station does not end the same
 * way a route to a system does. A route to a station ends inside it: the
 * last marker offers Dock, and an empty route with the ship still adrift
 * is a leg not yet finished. A route to a system ends in open space with
 * nothing further to press: the route empties itself on arrival and there
 * is no station to wait for.
 *
 * Which of the two applies is read off _state — what was actually ordered,
 * written by warp_choice.after_chosen the moment open_route_menu_and_warp
 * chooses Dock from the route marker's own menu — not off destination_kind
 * or return_kind. Those are the operator's own text fields, and the first
 * live mission this fix was built for set no route itself at all: another
 * bot (agent-missions) laid the route, this one only flew it, and
 * destination_kind sat at its default ("system") whether or not the route
 * it never wrote actually ended at a station. Gating on that default would
 * have declared the mission over the instant the route ran out, in open
 * space, Dock never even ordered — the same silent wrong answer the exit
 * condition used to give the other way round, just for the opposite kind
 * of leg. _state answers the only question that matters and cannot be
 * stale about it: was a dock actually asked for on the way here.
 *
 * Requiring a dock regardless of what was actually ordered left a
 * system-kind leg — the default this bot ships with — circling an empty
 * route forever after a live mission on 2026-08-09 flew exactly that route
 * and arrived. Everything else is Running: the tree keeps ticking and the
 * ship keeps moving.
 *
 * Idempotent by construction: with no route set the exit condition holds on
 * the first tick and the command is done without touching anything.
 *
 * The exit condition below is not reached every tick the way its comment
 * might suggest. It sits as the second child of a plain (memoryless)
 * Sequence, and neurofolia's Sequence stops at the first child that is not
 * Success (sequence.rs) — so on any tick where the body above answers
 * Running (open_route_menu_and_warp does, for as long as there is
 * something to try ordering), this condition is never ticked at all,
 * whatever it would have said. It is reached only on the tick the body's
 * own Fallback fails outright — nothing left anywhere for it to attempt —
 * and @fail_is_success turns that Failure into the Success that lets this
 * Sequence continue (fallback.rs). Confirmed against those two files and
 * against tree.rs, which ticks the root exactly once per iteration: this
 * is not a guess about the DSL's intent, it is what the engine actually
 * does. */

-> fly_route {
    @repeat_until_success -> {
        @fail_is_success -> {
            @! is_docking?()
            @! is_undocking?()
            ? {
                @if(push_button_yes) push_message_boxes
                on_space
                on_station
            }
        }
        /* exit condition */
        -> {
            ? {
                @! is_state?("dock")
                in_station?()
            }
            @! is_route_set?()
        }
    }
}
-> push_message_boxes {
    is_message_boxes?()
    push_message_boxes()
}
/* Undocking is pressed only from a hangar the client is showing. The three
   guards this replaces — no session change, in a station, and three seconds
   since the last press — were all trying to say that, and the timer was there
   because "in a station" stayed true for a moment after the press. The phase
   goes to undocking the instant the client announces it. */
-> on_station {
    phase_is?("docked")
    is_route_set?()
    push_undock_button()
}
/* The survey comes last of the three on purpose. move is the flight itself and
   outranks everything here; the cloak is next, because a ship that should be
   hidden should be hidden before it is inventoried; the survey takes what is
   left, which in warp is every tick. It answers Running for the twenty-odd
   ticks of a walk, and that is why it may not stand ahead of either: a fallback
   stops at the first child that is not Failure.

   Its own two guards — the mission asked for it, and the ship is actually in
   warp — are inside the action rather than here, unlike the cloak's phase_is
   just below. Not for taste: an action is what a case can tick, and "asked for
   but not flying yet" is exactly the state that has to be pinned by one. See
   survey_ship.lua. */
-> on_space {
    @! phase_is?("docked")
    ? {
        move
        @if(stealth) stealth
        survey_ship(survey_ship, remember_module_names)
    }
}
/* One phase says all of it: in space, nothing announced, no manoeuvre under
   way — the ship is free and an order given now will be taken. The five
   guards this replaces could each say what was not happening; none could say
   the client was ready, so between them sat a three-second timer guessing. */
-> move {
    /* session is here on trial: the client is said to refuse context menus
       while it changes, and the wait costs nine seconds after every jump.
       The action probes once per session change and reports what happened;
       if the claim holds, this word comes back out. */
    phase_is?("adrift", "session")
    ? {
        @if(bookmark_jump) dock_bookmark
        @if(bookmark_jump) undock_bookmark
        open_route_menu_and_warp()
    }
}
/* The wait that stood here as a condition has moved into the action, where
   every other press in this bot is spaced. The wait itself stays — it guards
   a toggle rather than an order, and F1 pressed twice uncloaks the ship it
   just cloaked — but the tree is no place for it: the tree asks what is true,
   and how long a press is given to land is the action's business. With it
   goes the last timer told in whole seconds off the wall clock.

   What is left is what a tree is for: not cloaked already, and in warp. */
-> stealth {
    @! is_stealth?()
    phase_is?("warping")
    stealth()
}
-> dock_bookmark {
    is_state?("warp")
    is_last_system?()
    open_dock_bookmarks_menu_and_warp()
}
-> undock_bookmark {
    is_state?("undock")
    open_undock_bookmarks_menu_and_warp()
}
